note[RIDL-406]: signal payload `EnvelopeEcho` declares `frameCounter`, which the envelope already carries — every publication is delivered with a timestamp and a sequence number, so the payload need not re-declare them (ridl §3.1). Domain metadata distinct from transport metadata is legitimate: keep the field if it records when the fact occurred rather than when it was published, or if it counts the fact itself rather than the publication carrying it.
   ┌─ tests/corpus/ridl-diag-showcase/main/lints.ridl:15:17
   │
15 │   signal echo : EnvelopeEcho @[1s..10s]
   │                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^

